# .gitignore — production/src/
#
# Template-owned; copier update keeps it current. Project-wide rules belong in the root .gitignore.
# No inline comments in this file: Git reads a # after a pattern as part of the pattern.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Masters, card renders and working copies
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Built by the toolkit from the tracked edit decision lists, cards, footage manifest, voiceover
# registers and timing and scene files: regenerable, and too large for plain Git. Each piece's
# renders sit in a folder named for it (renders/<piece>/, with its cards/, timing/, scene/ and
# stills/), and brand-kit proofs in renders/proofs/; the pattern below ignores every folder
# inside renders/ whole, so a per-piece folder needs no pattern of its own. The README stays
# tracked, so the folder and its note on what lands in it survive a fresh clone. The tracked
# timing/ and scenes/ folders beside renders/ are never ignored: no rule here touches them.
/renders/*
!/renders/README.md

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The local mirror of source media
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Footage lives in external storage by decision and is listed, with its checksum, in
# footage/manifest.toml; raw/ holds this machine's copies, which footage verify proves.
/footage/raw/*
!/footage/raw/README.md

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated voiceover
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ElevenLabs takes: paid for, impossible to make again identically, and too large for plain
# Git. An approved take is archived as source media, never committed. A piece's takes sit in
# voiceover/generated/<piece>/takes/ and its scratch tracks in <piece>/, and voice trials in
# voice-trials/<name>/; the pattern below ignores every folder inside generated/ whole. Takes
# an earlier release left flat at the folder's top are ignored the same way.
/voiceover/generated/*
!/voiceover/generated/README.md

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated narration and mastered chapters
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Chapter text chunks, their takes and the mastered chapters. The rules sit here rather than
# inside audiobook/ because production/src/ ships with every project: removing the audiobook
# media kind removes the template's files from audiobook/ but keeps your chapter registers and
# any audio beside them, and these rules go on keeping that audio and that text out of Git.
/audiobook/generated/*
!/audiobook/generated/README.md
/audiobook/renders/*
!/audiobook/renders/README.md
